# `comms::timing`

The timing offset of a shaped waveform.

## Signature

```cpp
pluss::Series comms::timing(const pluss::Series& waveform, std::int64_t samples_per_symbol);
```

## What It Does

Estimates the fractional symbol-timing offset in samples by the Oerder-Meyr square-law method: the squared magnitude of a pulse-shaped waveform has a tone at the symbol rate whose phase gives the offset. It needs no knowledge of the symbols.

## Parameters

`waveform`
: The received waveform, a real or complex `[..., L]` array holding at least four symbols.

`samples_per_symbol`
: The oversampling factor, at least `4`.

## Returns

A real array of shape `[...]`, in samples, in `(-samples_per_symbol / 2, samples_per_symbol / 2]`. A waveform delayed by `d` samples gives `d`, modulo one symbol.

## Errors

Throws `pluss::Error` for `samples_per_symbol` below `4` or a waveform shorter than four symbols.

## Interpretation and Use

Remove the estimate with `delay` before `match`, or sample at the estimated instants. The estimate improves with the length of the block and degrades gracefully with noise; a roll-off near zero weakens the tone.

